1.22.0: the raw door cuts to the image area

Sensors read out masked (optically black) columns and rows around the
picture, and the raw door handed them over: a D610 NEF came out
6080x4028 with a 64-column black stripe down one side, where every
other converter gives 6016x4016. The decoder now cuts the samples to
the image area before demosaic, statistics or anything else sees them:
DNG's ActiveArea and DefaultCropOrigin/Size (parsed before, never
applied), and for NEF the CropHiSpeed tag in the Nikon MakerNote,
which names the full readout, the picture size and its offset. A crop
at an odd offset shifts the CFA phase and the per-cell black level
with it. ProRAW DNGs carry no crop and are unchanged; 8-bit input is
untouched.

Two synthetic files join tests/raw: the uncompressed Bayer DNG inside
a larger readout with ActiveArea at (1,3), and the NEF inside a
readout with masked columns right and rows bottom, CropHiSpeed naming
the picture at (6,2). Both must decode to the bit as the plain files.
tools/make_test_raws.py regenerates all of them; the earlier files are
byte-identical to before.

Also in this release: the guarded _DARWIN_C_SOURCE defines, the quiet
serve-test cleanup and the fake-DOM localStorage (1.21.2).

